<title>PORTUGAL: Jeronimo Martins sales rose 28 pct-paper.</title>
<headline>Jeronimo Martins sales rose 28 pct-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese retailer Estabelecimentos Jeronimo Martins &amp; Filho SGPS boosted consolidated sales 27.7 percent to 359.6 billion escudos ($2.25 billion) in 1996 compared with a year earlier, Diario Economico reported on Tuesday, quoting a company source.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Sales were 438 billion escudos on a non-consolidated basis, the paper said.</p>
<p>($1=158.08 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035.</p>
</text>
